            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The edit correctly incorporates the governing statutory limitation from paragraph (5), which specifies that nothing in the section allows an individual access to information compiled in reasonable anticipation of a civil action or proceeding, into the access requirement of paragraph (1). The resulting reading is complete, accurate, and independently usable.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F001\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed summary erroneously claims that the agency must require every individual, whether accompanied or unaccompanied, to furnish written authorization before access. Under paragraph (1), the agency has discretionary authority ('may require') to require a written statement authorizing discussion only in the accompanying person's presence.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The unchanged draft omits the governing statutory limitation set forth in paragraph (5), which explicitly restricts access under this section for information compiled in reasonable anticipation of a civil action or proceeding, leaving the reading incomplete for independent use.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
